" :answer/id #uuid "a905265a-fa93-53e6-b47b-fff163dec00a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343443/field-4/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "b275aaa5-73de-5b07-ba9c-00afcf7af5a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343443/field-4/6d0086fbf1d5dadda84b813260fdcf9f8964549bf3d2a02972d43bc272b01425" :answer/id #uuid "53f6ac6d-4768-5a8c-8226-b2ade340221f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343443/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "233eb0a3-1d6f-52e2-9e32-154c1680b7bc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343443/field-4/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-343443/field-4/b627bdd0369562afa8f12be8f167039ff5f7a2bdc550b832dce7f5205e0a89bc" "q-343443/field-4/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-343443/field-4/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-343443/field-4/6d0086fbf1d5dadda84b813260fdcf9f8964549bf3d2a02972d43bc272b01425"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343443" :question/id #uuid "3f30ec43-27bd-57e4-8325-81a7fa57b09b" :question/math-academy-id "q-343443" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}3, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ -5, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{16}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1-\\frac{16}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-n\\pi )=(-1)^{n}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-1-\\frac{16}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\ 3 & =-1-\\frac{16}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n} \\\\ 4 & =-\\frac{16}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343443/field-1" "q-343443/field-2" "q-343443/field-3" "q-343443/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3cb7656-1ce6-5b6a-9e88-5ba24a943c3f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343443"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
